--- a/docs/src/content/docs/producer/author-primitives/prompts.md
+++ b/docs/src/content/docs/producer/author-primitives/prompts.md
@@ -34,9 +34,11 @@ what `apm init` scaffolds.
 
 ## Frontmatter
 
-Five keys are preserved by the cross-tool transform. Anything else
-is dropped at compile time and surfaced via diagnostics so consumers
-on lossy targets see a warning, not silent data loss.
+The cross-tool transform preserves five keys. Claude command files accept
+the same frontmatter as Claude skills, except `name` and `paths`; APM also
+preserves Claude's documented native fields only for Claude output. Other
+targets keep the cross-tool transform and report unsupported keys through
+diagnostics.
 
 | Key | Type | Purpose |
 |---|---|---|
@@ -46,6 +48,15 @@ on lossy targets see a warning, not silent data loss.
 | `model` | string | Preferred model slug (Claude/Cursor only). |
 | `argument-hint` | string | Free-form hint shown in the picker; auto-derived from `input` when omitted. |
 
+Claude additionally accepts `when_to_use`, `arguments`,
+`disable-model-invocation`, `user-invocable`, `disallowed-tools`, `effort`,
+`context`, `agent`, `background`, `hooks`, `shell`, `metadata`, `license`,
+and `compatibility`. See the
+[Claude Code frontmatter reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills#frontmatter-reference)
+for field semantics. Claude `hooks` frontmatter is subject to APM's existing
+package hook-approval gate: when hooks are not approved, APM withholds the
+field and reports a warning.
+
 Reference inputs in the body with `${input:name}`. The compiler
 rewrites these per target (for example, `$name` for Claude
 commands).
@@ -126,11 +137,12 @@ the parameter bound and invokes the harness. See
 
 ## Pitfalls
 
-- **Non-preserved frontmatter is dropped.** Keys like `author`,
-  `mcp`, or `parameters` survive on Copilot (verbatim copy) but are
-  stripped on Claude/Cursor/OpenCode/Gemini/Grok Build/Windsurf. APM logs a
-  diagnostic at install time. Keep authoritative metadata to the
-  five preserved keys.
+- **Target-specific frontmatter is not portable.** Claude-only fields
+  survive on Claude commands but are dropped on Cursor, OpenCode, Gemini,
+  Grok Build, and Windsurf. Unsupported fields such as `author`, `mcp`,
+  `parameters`, and Claude command-incompatible `name` or `paths` are
+  dropped on transformed targets with an install-time diagnostic. Copilot
+  receives the source file verbatim.
 - **Input names must match `[A-Za-z][\w-]{0,63}`.** Other entries
   are rejected with a warning at integrate time and never reach the
   command frontmatter.
